W: 6. Mirrored in nuptial purity 
W: The marriage of the Church we see 
W: And Christ the Bridegroom's Love; 
W: Angels look down, and anthems sing, 
W: The Holy Dove, the golden wing, 
W: Sheds blessings from above. 
W: 
W: 7. Bless these Thy servants, gracious Lord, 
W: Whom Thou dost join in sweet accord, 
W: The bridegroom and the bride; 
W: In sorrow, sickness, and in health 
W: In tribulation and in wealth, 
W: Be Thou their Help and Guide! 
W: 
W: 8. Be with them, Lord, as day by day 
W: They with one heart together pray, 
W: Thy Word together read, 
W: Together at Thine altar kneel, 
W: And with Thy Blood their union seal, 
W: On Thee together feed. 
W: 
W: 9. May they forever have Thee near, 
W: Making them to Thyself more dear, 
W: And each to each in Thee; 
W: So, when from earthly cares released, 
W: May they at Thine own marriage feast 
W: Be blest eternally! 
W: 
W: 10. $1D$2 To Father, whose paternal Love 
W: Sends benedictions from above, 
W: Eternal praises be; 
W: And God the Son, Incarnate Word, 
W: With Holy Spirit be adored; 
W: One God and Persons Three! 

